# Committed image fixtures are binary evidence for the decode tests
# (MULTIMODAL_INPUT_IMPLEMENTATION.md S01). Without this rule `corrupt.png`
# — a PNG signature followed by 0xFF bytes, no NULs — is guessed to be text
# and autocrlf rewrites its CRLF pair, changing the bytes under test.
# The real image formats are detected as binary on their own; the rule
# keeps them that way regardless of content.
test/fixtures/images/* binary
